  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct, so none were added or dropped.",
   "The piezo disc is catalogue type 'buzzer'. Pin 2 (+) goes to A0 through the red wire and pin 1 (-) goes to GND through the black wire, as the card says.",
   "The 1 Megohm resistor is in parallel with the piezo. Column 5 joins piezo pin 1, the resistor and the black GND wire. Column 8 joins piezo pin 2, the resistor and the red A0 wire. This matches the schematic.",
   "The image shows the breadboard with rows f-j in the upper half. I used the catalogue hole naming, where bank 'b' means rows f-j, and put the parts in columns 5 and 8 of rows f-j (piezo in row i, resistor in row h, black wire in row g, red wire in row f).",
   "The black wire goes to the GND pin next to pin 13 and AREF. I called it GND.1.",
   "The schematic shows a 5V pin at the top of the Arduino, but no wire connects to it, so no 5V connection is made."
  ]
 },
